0688                         **     BREAKPOINT RETURN
0689                         *
0690                         *        'GO' COMMAND HANDLER HAS SETUP UP SYSTEM
0691                         *          SWIVECTOR to HERE IF THERE ARE ANY
0692                         *            BREAKPOINTS. WE MUST EXAMINE BREAKPOINT
0693                         *              TABLE TO SEE IF SWI IS BREAKPOINT OR
0694                         *                USER CODE. THE SWI MUST BE INTERPRETED
0695                         *                  IF IT IS PART OF USER CODE
0696                         
0697 fe3d 08                 GO3    INX
0698 fe3e 08                        INX
0699 fe3f 08                        INX
0700 fe40 6d 00                     TST    0,X      LOOK FOR LAST BREAKPOINT
0701 fe42 26 1e                     BNE    GO7
0702 fe44 8d 7b                     BSR    SSTEP    STEP PAST USER SWI
0703 fe46 ce fe 4f                  LDX    #GO5
0704 fe49 bf dd f2           GO4    STS    TEM1
0705 fe4c 7e ff 24                  JMP    SWIVE1
0706 fe4f 30                 GO5    TSX             RETURN HERE ON BREAKPOINT
0707 fe50 bf dd f0                  STS    USERS
0708 fe53 be dd f2                  LDS    TEM1
0709 fe56 a6 06                     LDAA   6,X      DECREMENT USER PC
0710 fe58 26 02                     BNE    GO6        AND SAVE A COPY IN (BA)
0711 fe5a 6a 05                     DEC    5,X
0712 fe5c e6 05              GO6    LDAB   5,X
0713 fe5e 4a                        DECA
0714 fe5f a7 06                     STAA   6,X
0715 fe61 30                        TSX
0716 fe62 e1 01              GO7    CMPB   1,X      SEARCH STACK FOR BREAKPOINT
0717 fe64 26 d7                     BNE    GO3
0718 fe66 a1 02                     CMPA   2,X
0719 fe68 26 d3                     BNE    GO3
0720 fe6a bd fd a6                  JSR CRLF
0721 fe6d bd fc a7                  JSR    REGS     PRINT USER REGISTERS
0722 fe70 20 a6                     BRA    RESET2
